y Miriodor.","color":"#38bdf8","family":"Progresivo, krautrock y jazz-rock","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#neo-prog"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":267597729004128,"artist":"Ozric Tentacles","artist_id":193248221396770,"title":"Pungent Effulgent","year":1989,"ess":0,"yt":null,"kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Neo-progresivo","scene_id":150113334913508,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#neo-prog","chapters":["Sección 5.12"],"pages":[[1,164,null]]},{"id":12686589132828,"artist":"Ozric Tentacles","artist_id":193248221396770,"title":"Erpland","year":1990,"ess":1,"yt":"pJIb_4MvVZ4","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Neo-progresivo","scene_id":150113334913508,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#neo-prog","chapters":["Sección 5.12"],"pages":[[1,164,null]]},{"id":162675462601285,"artist":"Ozric Tentacles","artist_id":193248221396770,"title":"Strangeitude","year":1991,"ess":0,"yt":"QTEN5Fnnbek","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Neo-progresivo","scene_id":150113334913508,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#neo-prog","chapters":["Sección 5.12"],"pages":[[1,164,null]]},{"id":111388520470819,"artist":"Ozric Tentacles","artist_id":193248221396770,"title":"Jurassic Shift","year":1993,"ess":0,"yt":"fJvVXfqyLRM","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Neo-progresivo","scene_id":150113334913508,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#neo-prog","chapters":["Sección 5.12"],"pages":[[1,164,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":164,"text":"…and lengthy suites, but subsequent albums simply aimed for pop mainstream. The psychedelic movement lent England its best progressive bands. The Ozric Tentacles (13), \"the\" progressive band of the 1990s (although it began releasing cassettes in the mid 1980s), took Gong's legacy (fusing jazz-rock, hard-rock…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":164,"text":"…ensemble (including two electronic keyboards, a sampler, four percussionists, flute, bass and guitar) and displaying an almost baroque elegance. The Ozric Tentacles had mastered, at the same time, the melodic ingenuity of classical music, the fluidity of jazz-rock and the drive of hard-rock. The sound was so…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":232,"text":"…documented on Soulcraft (1993), that were the ultimate cybernetic-psychedelic ragas. Falcone's own Melting Euphoria were disciples of the Ozric Tentacles' cosmic-progressive rock. International progressive 1992-96 In France, Philharmonie experimented with the unusual format of a guitar trio,…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":263,"text":"…In Sides (1996) turned to narrative logic and emotional content, using the dance beats as mere background. Eat Static (2), a side project of Ozric Tentacles' drummer Merv Pepler and keyboardist Joie Hinton, used techno beats to reach the same orbit as Gong's effervescent space-hippie prog-rock. The craft…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":174172693890104,"type":"album","name":"Erpsongs","list_id":28712889142764,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Jam Band","src":"musthear","rank":105,"year":1985,"note":null,"yt":"xkIB1WorE88","scaruffi":null},{"id":92575986548394,"type":"album","name":"Tantric Obstacles","list_id":28712889142764,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Jam Band","src":"musthear","rank":120,"year":1985,"note":null,"yt":"6KviIdlhPuA","scar